<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-compōno</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				pŏsĭtum, 3, v.
			a.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to put together
			again</i>, <i>to reunite</i>, <i>rearrange</i>, <i>readjust</i> (rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 7, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lapillos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 2, 25 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fracturam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 3, 47, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to soothe
			again</i>, <i>recall to composure</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 6,
				5, 5</span></i>. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
